From 2f5029dc0ef3175f13e7428f018465f9f6c98449 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Edwards <jeff@edwardsj.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:37:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: packet sockets for a device kept from the network stack

With HERMIT_RAW_MAC set (env=HERMIT_RAW_MAC=xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx on the
command line), the virtio-net device with that MAC address is never
given to smoltcp. Instead socket(AF_PACKET=5, SOCK_RAW) hands its whole
Ethernet frames to one application at a time: read() returns one frame,
write() sends one. The first other device serves the network stack as
before, and any further one is left unused, so the kernel never moves a
frame between the two devices. An unparsable HERMIT_RAW_MAC stops the
boot rather than give the device to the stack.

Gated behind the net-packet feature (virtio-net over PCI).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
